{
  "raw": {
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Events-Coordinator_R003381": {
      "title": "Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Events Coordinator Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Conference and Event Services Job Summary: This is a professional position reporting to the Director of Conference & Event Services. This person is responsible for sales, event booking and event management at the Younts Conference Center. Responsibilities include client services, collaboration with other university departments, and client-level operational support of in-house technology at the Younts Center. This employee is responsible for administrative and operational coordination of events at the Younts Conference Center and weddings at various campus locations. Job Description: Job Responsibilities Operations Coordinate with university and off-campus clients to determine event space, technical, and logistical needs. Prepare setup plans for events; communicate plans and revisions to clients and production staff. Coordinate with university departments and vendors to secure resources and staff support for events. Act as \"manager on duty\" for Younts Center and other campus events. Promptly address client concerns during events, utilizing departmental, university and vendor resources as appropriate. Provide on call support for summer clients during their time on campus. Communicate and enforce safety and facility policies. Conduct ongoing review of facility operations to ensure compliance with safety procedures.. Administration Maintain current information on university facilities and vendors for dissemination to potential clients. Schedule events at the Younts Center and campus wedding venues. Enter and update client information and event bookings in EBMS and R25.; resolve booking conflict& with other departmental and university events. Generate contracts, cost estimates & invoices for events. Receive and process contracts and certificates of insurance. Receive payments & forward appropriately for processing. Provide event & incident reports to the Director and, as appropriate, other university departments & external agencies. Consultation Serve as a consultant for university departments & organizations planning events not held in spaces administered by the department. Develop professional, cooperative relationships with faculty, staff, student & community constituencies. T. Facility Upkeep Monitor equipment conditions and behavior; troubleshoot equipment and, when necessary, refer to appropriate departments/vendors  for resolution. Employee Development Communicate openly & effectively with and recognize the contributions of supervisors & co-workers. Complete performance review process. Pursue professional development to enhance work performance. Work Relationships The Event Coordinator maintains a generally cooperative attitude and continuous contact with the Director, others in Conference & Event Services, members of other departments, and professional & student staff for planning, coordinating, problem solving, presenting information and suggestions relating to mutual goals. This person frequently contacts students and the general public to exchange factual information and explain rules, regulations, practices and functions. Decision-Making & Accountability This person reviews ongoing and completed work to ensure compliance with procedures and deadlines. Job tasks involve multiple procedures with interrelated processes or steps.  This person's work involves choosing the appropriate option(s) or procedure(s) to follow and applying established rules and procedures. Supervision The Event Coordinator reports to the Director of Conference & Event Services. This person performs work independently in routine matters and refers non-routine issues or questions to the Director. Education/Skill Requirements Bachelor's  degree with 1-3 years' experience in related field required. Sales and event experience, preferably in the hospitality industry, is preferred. The successful candidate will demonstrate professional experience and superior skills in communication, organization, and administration, along with commitment to excellent client service.  Computer proficiency (Windows and Microsoft Office suite) is required. The successful candidate will demonstrate comfort working in a fast-paced, team environment. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to take initiative and work independently. Work Conditions This position requires: Multitasking and prioritization of multiple ongoing processes; Configuration, use and troubleshooting of computer, audio-visual and related technology; Frequent use of office computer, telecommunication  and document handling equipment. Frequent standing and walking in indoor and outdoor event, athletic and housing venues; Occasional reaching and handling of tools & objects; Occasional stooping, kneeling, crouching and crawling; occasional pushing and pulling, lifting and carrying, climbing and balancing; Frequent exposure to extremes of temperature & weather during outdoor events and summer programs; Evening and weekend work. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Groundskeeper_R003382": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Groundskeeper Job Family: Service Workers Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Hourly Department: Athletic Grounds Job Summary: The Groundskeeper position is responsible for maintaining the appearance, safety, and functionality of campus and/or athletic grounds. This position performs routine and seasonal landscaping, grounds maintenance, and irrigation work to ensure an attractive and welcoming campus environment for students, staff, and visitors. Job Description: Essential Duties and Responsibilities Grounds and Turf Maintenance •Mow, edge, and trim campus lawns using tractor mowers, push mowers, gang mowers, and hand tools. •Operate weed eaters, edgers, clippers, and backpack blowers. •Perform aeration, sodding, seeding, fertilizing, and irrigation of turf areas. •Collect and dispose of litter, fallen limbs, leaves, and debris. •Apply fertilizers, herbicides, and pesticides in accordance with safety standards and regulations. •Clear overgrown areas using bush hogs or other appropriate equipment. Landscape, Tree, and Plant Care •Prune and trim shrubs, flowers, and trees using hand tools, power equipment, chainsaws, ladders, or bucket trucks. •Plant, transplant, and remove flowers, shrubs, and trees using hand tools or heavy equipment. •Mulch and weed flower beds and landscaped areas. •Remove tree stumps and unwanted vegetation using stump grinders, backhoes, or other equipment. •Identify plant disease, pest issues, or safety concerns and report them to supervision. Walkways, Parking Lots, and Water Features •Maintain cleanliness of sidewalks, parking lots, roads, and common areas by blowing or vacuuming debris. •Clean storm drains and drainage systems to prevent blockages. •Maintain campus lake and surrounding areas by removing debris and assisting with injured wildlife using approved methods and equipment. •Remove snow and ice from walkways and entrances as needed. Equipment and Irrigation Maintenance •Clean, inspect, and perform basic maintenance on grounds equipment and vehicles. •Sharpen blades and check oil, fuel, and filters. •Assist Irrigation Technician with repairing irrigation systems, including sprinkler heads, valves, pipes, and controllers. Professional Responsibilities •Follow all safety procedures and proper use of personal protective equipment (PPE). •Communicate effectively with supervisors, coworkers, students, and the public. •Participate in performance reviews and contribute to department and university goals. •Pursue ongoing professional development related to grounds maintenance and landscaping. •Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor. Relationships and Communication •Regular interaction with immediate supervisor and work unit to exchange information and coordinate tasks. •Frequent contact with students, staff, and the general public to provide information and assistance related to campus grounds. Decision-Making Authority •Performs assigned tasks following established procedures and guidelines. •Selects appropriate tools and equipment for routine work. •Completed work is reviewed by the supervisor. Education and Experience Requirements •High school diploma or equivalent. •One to two (1–2) years of experience in groundskeeping, landscaping, or a related field. •Valid South Carolina driver’s license. •Ability to read and understand instructions for equipment operation, chemicals, and materials. •Experience operating grounds maintenance tools and equipment. •Horticulture degree or equivalent experience preferred. Work Conditions and Physical Requirements •Work is performed primarily outdoors in varying weather conditions. •Regular exposure to noise, dust, heat, cold, chemicals, and fumes. •Frequent lifting and carrying of equipment and materials up to 70 pounds. •Frequent bending, stooping, reaching, pushing, pulling, and walking. •Regular operation of mowers, tractors, blowers, weed eaters, and hand tools. On-Call Responsibilities Groundskeepers may be subject to call-back during emergencies, including downed trees, snow and/or ice removal, or special events on campus. Reports To: Senior Groundskeeper, Assistant Superintendent of Campus Grounds/Athletic Grounds and Superintendent of Grounds, Horticulture, and Sports Turf Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Writer---Media-Relations-Specialist_R003380": {
      "title": "Writer & Media Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Writer & Media Relations Specialist Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Strategic Communications Job Summary: As a member of University Marketing & Communications at Furman University, the Writer & Media Relations Specialist is responsible for writing and editing news content, feature stories and copy across multiple mediums, and for proactive and responsive Media Relations with the goal of illustrating the impact of Furman University and its students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors and the broader community. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist creates and edits content for a wide range of print and digital communications, including magazine stories, news releases, marketing and advertising materials, web and social content, internal communications and presentations — adapting tone, format and length to fit the platform and the audience, from a long-form magazine feature to a short-form social caption built for the scroll. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist reports to the Director of Content Strategy and partners with departmental leadership, faculty and staff of the university in developing story ideas and editorial strategy. In addition to storytelling, the Writer & Media Relations Specialist provides daily media relations support under the direction of the Vice President and Assistant Vice President for University Communications — serving as a steady, trusted voice for Furman with reporters and media outlets, and helping protect and build the university’s reputation with both internal and external audiences. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist collaborates with all members of the University Marketing & Communications team, and with Furman faculty and staff, to deliver creative, accurate and compelling stories. The Writer & Media Relations Specialist is a proven expert in Associated Press style, feature writing and news writing, with the versatility to write well for any channel Furman’s story needs to reach. Job Description: Responsibilities Storytelling & Content Creation Write and edit news content, feature stories, profiles and institutional narratives that illustrate the impact of Furman University and its people. Create and edit copy for a wide range of print and digital communications, including magazine stories, news releases, marketing and advertising materials, internal communications and executive presentations. Interview faculty, staff, students, alumni and donors to source original, accurate and compelling stories. Apply Associated Press style consistently, along with Furman’s house style and editorial standards, across all written content. Media Relations & Reputation Provide daily media relations support on behalf of the university, under the direction of the Assistant Vice President for University Communications — including responding to reporter inquiries, coordinating interview requests and drafting statements and talking points. Serve as a trusted, front-line point of contact for media, representing Furman with professionalism, accuracy and care in every interaction. Monitor daily news and media coverage of Furman, proactively flagging emerging stories, risks and opportunities to the Assistant Vice President and Director of Content Strategy. Help shape and protect Furman’s reputation with both internal audiences (faculty, staff, students) and external audiences (media, prospective students, alumni, donors and the broader public), ensuring consistent, accurate messaging across every touchpoint. Support the university’s response to sensitive or time-sensitive situations by drafting clear, accurate communications quickly, escalating appropriately to the Assistant Vice President. Multi-Channel & Digital Adaptation Adapt stories and messaging across mediums — print, web, social, video scripts and advertising — tailoring tone, length and format to fit each platform and audience. Write and edit web and social copy with an understanding of how content is discovered and consumed online, including search visibility (SEO/AEO/GEO) and platform-specific best practices for social and digital engagement. Draft scripts and copy for video, podcast and other emerging storytelling formats as Furman’s communications channels evolve. Use available data and performance insights — in partnership with digital and marketing colleagues — to inform how stories are framed, formatted and distributed across channels. Editorial Collaboration & Strategy Partner with the Director of Content Strategy and UMC leadership to develop story ideas, editorial calendars and content strategy that align with institutional priorities. Collaborate with colleagues across University Marketing & Communications — including design, digital strategy and social media — to ensure stories are told cohesively across every channel. Work closely with Furman faculty, staff and campus partners to identify newsworthy stories and ensure accuracy and appropriate context in coverage. Contribute to brainstorming and planning for major institutional storytelling initiatives, campaigns and special publications. Brand Voice & Editorial Standards Adapt the tone of writing to ensure messages are effectively targeted toward specific audiences — prospective students, alumni, donors, faculty/staff or the broader public — while maintaining a consistent institutional voice. Serve as a steward of Furman’s editorial voice and style standards, helping ensure consistency across contributors and channels. Fact-check and proofread content to ensure accuracy, clarity and adherence to AP and Furman house style. Professional Practice Manage multiple writing assignments and deadlines simultaneously in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Use generative AI tools responsibly and selectively — for research support, brainstorming or first-draft acceleration — while ensuring all published work reflects original reporting, editorial judgment and Furman’s authentic voice. Stay current on trends in journalism, digital storytelling and higher education communications, bringing fresh ideas back to the team. Perform other duties as assigned. Experience and Required Skills Bachelor’s degree in journalism, English, communications or a related field. 5 or more years of professional writing and editing experience, preferably in journalism, higher education communications or content marketing. Proven expertise in Associated Press style, feature writing and news writing. Experience providing media relations support — responding to reporter inquiries, drafting statements and talking points, and representing an organization’s voice accurately and calmly under deadline pressure. Demonstrated ability to write effectively across multiple formats and platforms — print, web, social, video scripts and advertising copy. Working understanding of how content performs across digital and social platforms, and comfort adapting long-form writing for short-form, platform-native consumption. Familiarity with generative AI tools and their appropriate, responsible use in a writing and editorial workflow. Excellent interviewing skills and the ability to build trust quickly with faculty, staff, students, alumni and donors. Strong collaborative instincts, with the ability to take and give constructive feedback across a team of writers, editors and designers. Exceptional attention to detail, with strong fact-checking and proofreading skills. Ability to manage multiple deadlines and shifting priorities in a fast-paced newsroom-style environment. Work Conditions Work is performed under usual office conditions. University Marketing & Communications Culture and Values Statement University Marketing & Communications’ values are grounded in professionalism, respect and humility. We are unified, driven and purposeful in pursuing our common goal of advancing Furman University. We approach every task as problem-solvers who are curious, creative and innovative — and good listeners first. We value each other’s talents, and understand that achieving excellence requires care and attention to the personal growth and well-being of each member of our team. At the end of the day, our work should be fun, engaging and inspiring — and create advocates across the Furman community and beyond. Application Requirements Resume Cover letter Writing samples (a mix of long-form and short-form/digital work is preferred) These should be attached as a single PDF Candidates selected for interviews will be expected to discuss their editorial process, experience adapting stories across platforms, and examples of storytelling that required close collaboration with subjects or campus partners. Education Requirements: Bachelors Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Athletics-Director---Graphic-Design---Social-Media_R003370": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletics Director - Graphic Design & Social Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant Athletics Director - Graphic Design & Social Media Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Athletic Director External Affairs Job Summary: This position serves as the Athletic Departments lead creative and social media professional and is responsible for graphic design, visual storytelling, illustration, print production, and digital content development for all 19 sports. The position leads the creation of high-quality, brand-aligned content that enhances the Athletics brand, supports recruiting and fan engagement, and advances departmental and university priorities across print, web, email, and social media platforms. Job Description: Essential Duties and Responsibilities Lead graphic design, visual storytelling, and creative content efforts for the Department of Athletics across all 19 sports, ensuring a consistent and professional brand presence. Create and produce a wide range of digital and print assets, including season graphics packages, recruiting materials, schedule graphics, web ads, email graphics, and other promotional materials. Develop and maintain the visual identity of Athletics across the website, official social media channels, digital campaigns, and external communications. Collaborate with coaches, communications staff, marketing staff, and other athletics personnel to create content that supports recruiting, brand growth, fan engagement, and sport-specific priorities. Manage the full design production process, including project timelines, art direction, photography coordination, print production, proofing, vendor communication, and related production tasks. Partner with creative video and external operations staff on video board assets, animation elements, motion graphics, and other multimedia needs. Provide guidance and daily oversight to student workers and other support personnel assisting with graphic design and social media content production. Manage multiple projects simultaneously, meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment, and remain current on emerging trends and best practices in design, branding, and digital media. Perform related duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility Provide guidance and oversight to student workers and other support personnel involved in creative content, graphic design, and social media production. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Graphic Design, Communications, Marketing, Fine Arts, Digital Media, Interdisciplinary Studies, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of 3 years of progressively responsible professional experience in graphic design, creative services, athletics communications, marketing, social media, or a related field. Preferred Qualifications Experience in collegiate athletics, professional sports, higher education, or a similarly fast-paced environment. Experience developing creative assets and social media content for multiple teams, brands, or audiences simultaneously. Demonstrated experience leading creative projects from concept through final production. Experience supervising student workers, interns, or entry-level creative staff. Illustration, animation, motion graphics, photography, and/or videography experience. Familiarity with NCAA, conference, and university policies related to athletics communications, recruiting, and branding. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of graphic design, branding, visual communications, typography, layout, and creative production workflows. Knowledge of social media content design, digital storytelling, print production, and reproduction processes. Ability to create compelling visual content across a wide range of media and platforms. Ability to translate statistics and technical information into clear, engaging graphics. Ability to manage multiple deadlines, maintain brand consistency, and work effectively in a fast-paced environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, including Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Acrobat, and After Effects, as well as Microsoft Office. Ability to work outside normal business hours, including nights and weekends, as required. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Electrician_R003317": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Electrician Job Family: Service Workers Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Hourly Department: Electrical Shop Job Summary: To perform construction, installation, maintenance and repair of electrical systems, equipment and fixtures. Job Description: Responsibilities : 1.  Maintains all electrical systems and power supply throughout campus including: High-Voltage underground and overhead systems including transformers Low Standard Voltage Standard Voltage, Switchgear, Panels, Feeders and Branch Circuits Various types of electrical equipment. Generator Maintenance and Functional Testing. 2.  Performs installation and repair of wiring, electrical fixtures, and systems by: Reviewing diagrams and/or existing electrical systems. Measuring, cutting, bending, threading, assembling and installing electrical conduit using tools such as hacksaw, pipe threader, and conduit bender. Pulling wire through conduit with assistance. Splicing and termination of wires using standard industry methods. Connecting wiring to lighting fixtures and power equipment, using hand tools. Installing control and distribution apparatus; such as switches, relays, and circuit breaker panels; fastening them in place with screws or bolts, using drills, masonry chisels, hammer, anchor bolt and wrench. Connecting power cables to equipment and installing grounding leads. Testing continuity of circuits to ensure electrical compatibility and safety of all components, using standard instruments such as ohmmeter, meggar and oscilloscope. Observing functions of installed equipment or system to detect hazards and the need for adjustment, relocation or replacement. 3.  Maintains the power and lights at the stadium and other on-campus locations. 4.  Provides electrical and generator maintenance at the President’s home. 5.  Records name, completion date and time, and description of parts used on work orders. 6.  Locates and marks underground electrical conduit using locator and drawings. 7.  Operates various equipment including trenching equipment for new installations of underground power and lighting. 8. Completes job estimates and purchase order requests as required. 9. Supports special events. 10.  Assists electrical sub-contractors and other trades in Facilities Services on projects. 11.  Reviews plans and blueprints for take offs, upgrades drawings as projects are finished. 12.  Performs other duties as assigned by the supervisor. 13.  Follows safety procedures. 14. Completes performance review process with supervisor/employees to understand job performance expectations and how they fit into the department and university goals. 15.  Communicates openly and recognizes contributions of co-workers and supervisor. 16. Pursues professional development to keep pace with demands for services and information; including maintaining up to date information about the department and university. Relationships : Continuous contact with members of own work unit and immediate supervisor requiring planning, coordinating, problem solving, presenting information and suggestions related mutual goals.  Parties generally have cooperative attitudes. Frequent contact with members of other departments, students, general public requiring exchange of factual information and explanation of rules, regulation, practices or functions. Discussion of non-controversial matters. Responsibility for Final Decisions :     Tasks involve multiple procedures with interrelated processes or steps.  Work involves choosing the appropriate option or procedure to follow and applying established rules and procedures. Errors are readily detected in the normal course of work by standard check or crosscheck.  Causes little difficulty or loss of time to correct. Reports To :  Electrical Supervisor Completed work is referred to supervisor for review. Education/Skill Requirements : High School graduate with 1 - 2 years experience in related field. Ability to read and interpret instructions, descriptions and diagrams in equipment/system manuals. Knowledge of National Electrical Codes. Work Conditions: Work is performed both outside for stadium, lighting and outside units and inside with constant exposure to heat, cold, electrical currents. Continuous use of gears, knobs, levers, hand tools (screwdriver, testers, pliers, etc) to repair, install and operate electrical units. Work requires: Continuous crouching, crawling to access lights. Daily climbing of stairs and ladders to reach lights, circuitry. Frequent reaching to access lighting and circuitry at a distance and overhead. Frequent lifting of 10-20 lbs. Occasional use of bucket truck to reach outside lighting. On call 24 hours a day. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Deputy-General-Counsel_R003350": {
      "title": "Deputy General Counsel",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Deputy General Counsel Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: General Counsel Job Summary: The Deputy General Counsel will be a senior member of the Office of General Counsel and will serve as a key advisor to the Vice President and General Counsel. The successful candidate must be able to manage a demanding and wide-ranging practice, exercise sound legal and practical judgment, and communicate effectively with colleagues and clients. The candidate will be expected to handle significant and complex matters and transactions from beginning to end with minimal supervision. Job Description: JOB DESCRIPTION Principal Duties and Responsibilities Provide timely legal advice to university divisions on day-to-day matters pertaining to the operation of the university, including in particular those related to staff employment, tort liability, student issues, athletics, research and sponsored programs, and data privacy and security. Review, draft, and negotiate contracts on behalf of the University. Develop and maintain legal templates, forms, and guidance documents. Assist policy makers in drafting, revising, and implementing institutional policies and procedures and provide advice regarding the legal implications of institutional policies and initiatives. Coordinate litigation and other significant legal matters in consultation with the Vice President and General Counsel; gather information and manage discovery for litigation and administrative investigations. Manage responses to subpoenas, document requests, records inquiries, and data privacy requests in coordination with relevant offices. Conduct legal research and provide advice on legal and regulatory issues affecting the university. Provide guidance and support to other members of the Office of General Counsel, as appropriate, and contribute to the effective administration and operation of the office. Serve as the Vice President and General Counsel’s designee on University committees, working groups, and other institutional matters, as appropriate. In the absence of the Vice President and General Counsel, exercise such authority and responsibility as may be delegated by the Vice President and General Counsel. Maintain strong relationships across the University to provide accessible, solutions-oriented counsel that supports Furman’s mission and priorities. Work on special projects in response to needs as assigned by the General Counsel and perform duties as required and/or assigned by the VPGC. Qualifications Juris Doctor (J.D.) degree from an American Bar Association-accredited law school. Licensed to practice law in the State of South Carolina, or eligible for licensure within a reasonable time from the date of hire. A minimum of 5 years of recent experience as a practicing attorney, with substantial proficiency and depth in one or more of the following areas: drafting and negotiating sophisticated agreements, civil litigation, employment, research and sponsored programs, Division 1 college athletics, and/or privacy laws. A solid working knowledge of the legal, academic, and operational issues relevant to the operations of a liberal arts institution, with willingness to develop new subject matter expertise as client needs dictate . Experience in a college or university general counsel’s office is strongly preferred. Strong research and analytical skills, coupled with sound judgment and the ability to balance legal risks with other priorities. Capacity to thrive in a collaborative, collegial environment and work independently with a high degree of motivation. Demonstrated ability to handle multiple, unrelated matters concurrently and to perform effectively under the pressure of frequent interruptions, conflicting demands, and changing priorities. Demonstrated ability to identify potential legal issues and the long-term implications of policy and legal decisions. Demonstrated ability to establish relationships with various constituencies; work collaboratively to find solutions to very complex problems; and to lead and participate in complex projects requiring a team approach for resolution. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. High ethical standards, reflecting honesty, integrity, and reliability. Strong client service orientation and skills. Education Requirements: Juris Doctor (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Biology---Invertebrate-Zoology-Entomology--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003354": {
      "title": "Professor of Biology - Invertebrate Zoology/Entomology (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Biology - Invertebrate Zoology/Entomology (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Biology Job Summary: Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Biology at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor, beginning August 2027. Job Description: We seek a broadly trained biologist who is excited to teach across the undergraduate curriculum, mentor students in authentic research, and contribute to a collaborative liberal arts and sciences community. Teaching expectations for this position may include lecture and laboratory courses from a newly revised slate of introductory biology and data science courses. We are interested in recruiting candidates with expertise in teaching entomology and/or other areas of invertebrate biology. Candidates with expertise in related areas are also encouraged to apply. Other teaching responsibilities may include opportunities to develop new upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, especially those that broaden our current course offerings. The Department of Biology currently has 15 full-time Biology faculty members and offers both a B.A. and a B.S. degree in Biology. Furman University is located in the Piedmont of Upstate South Carolina near the Blue Ridge Mountains, which provides a rich environment for local field classes and research. In addition, the Department of Biology offers study away programs in Belize, Ecuador, New Mexico, and South Africa. The area of research specialization for this position is flexible, and we welcome applicants whose scholarship complements and extends the department’s current strengths. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a rigorous scholarly program that produces peer-reviewed work. Faculty in the Department of Biology are expected to engage with undergraduate students as collaborators in their scholarly work, which frequently involves summer research activities. Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and institutional financial support for faculty-mentored undergraduate research and student conference participation. The Department of Biology is housed with other sciences in the 200,000 square-foot Charles H. Townes Science Center. Faculty members have access to shared instrumentation that supports a broad range of research activities including microscopy (confocal, SEM), mammalian tissue-culture, molecular biology instrumentation (including thermal cyclers, qPCR system, DNA sequence analyzer, microplate readers for absorbance- and fluorescence-based spectrophotometry and digital gel and blot imaging systems), and an NIH-compliant animal facility. The Department of Biology also houses a BodyViz system (a 3D anatomy learning platform based on real patient CT and MRI data that allows students to virtually dissect hundreds of vertebrate bodies including humans and other animals) and several natural history collections (including a herbarium, a vertebrate collection, and an insect collection). For further information on our department, please visit https://www.furman.edu/academics/biology/ . Biologists whose work integrates views from multiple areas of biology and other science disciplines are particularly encouraged to apply. The strongest candidates will demonstrate an understanding of – and enthusiasm for – teaching and conducting research at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts institution, providing students with a rich and varied educational experience, and enhancing inclusion in STEM. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biology (or a related discipline) by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided that the degree is conferred by that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and postdoctoral experience are highly preferred but not required. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a cover letter describing your qualifications and identifying the position for which you are applying (2 pages max), a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages max), a statement of research priorities outlining your plan to mentor undergraduates in research activities (3 pages max), unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills, or demonstrate your efforts in these areas.   Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled.  Questions about this position may be directed to Dennis Haney, Professor of Biology (dennis.haney @furman.edu ) . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Biology---Anatomy--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003355": {
      "title": "Professor of Biology - Anatomy (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Biology - Anatomy (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Biology Job Summary: Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Biology at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor, beginning August 2027. Job Description: We seek a broadly trained biologist who is excited to teach across the undergraduate curriculum, mentor students in authentic research, and contribute to a collaborative liberal arts and sciences community. Teaching expectations for this position may include lecture and laboratory courses from a newly revised slate of introductory biology and data science courses. We are interested in recruiting candidates with expertise in teaching human anatomy and/or comparative anatomy. Candidates with expertise in related areas are also encouraged to apply. Other teaching responsibilities may include opportunities to develop new upper-level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, especially those that broaden our current course offerings. The Department of Biology currently has 15 full-time Biology faculty members and offers both a B.A. and a B.S. degree in Biology. Furman University is located in the Piedmont of Upstate South Carolina near the Blue Ridge Mountains , which provides a rich environment for local field classes and research. In addition, the Department of Biology offers study away programs in Belize, Ecuador, New Mexico, and South Africa.   The area of research specialization for this position is flexible, and we welcome applicants whose scholarship complements and extends the department’s current strengths. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain a rigorous scholarly program that produces peer-reviewed work. Faculty in the Department of Biology are expected to engage with undergraduate students as collaborators in their scholarly work, which frequently involves summer research activities. Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and institutional financial support for faculty-mentored undergraduate research and student conference participation. The Department of Biology is housed with other sciences in the 200,000 square-foot Charles H. Townes Science Center. Faculty members have access to shared instrumentation that supports a broad range of research activities including microscopy (confocal, SEM), mammalian tissue-culture, molecular biology instrumentation (including thermal cyclers, qPCR system, DNA sequence analyzer, microplate readers for absorbance- and fluorescence-based spectrophotometry and digital gel and blot imaging systems), and an NIH-compliant animal facility. The Department of Biology also houses a BodyViz system (a 3D anatomy learning platform based on real patient CT and MRI data that allows students to virtually dissect hundreds of vertebrate bodies including humans and other animals) and several natural history collections (including a herbarium, a vertebrate collection, and an insect collection). For further information on our department, please visit https://www.furman.edu/academics/biology/ .    Biologists whose work integrates views from multiple areas of biology and other science disciplines are particularly encouraged to apply. The strongest candidates will demonstrate an understanding of – and enthusiasm for – teaching and conducting research at a primarily undergraduate liberal arts institution, providing students with a rich and varied educational experience, and enhancing inclusion in STEM. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biology (or a related discipline) by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided that the degree is conferred by that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and postdoctoral experience are highly preferred but not required. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a cover letter describing your qualifications and identifying the position for which you are applying (2 pages max), a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy (2 pages max), a statement of research priorities outlining your plan to mentor undergraduates in research activities (3 pages max), unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills, or demonstrate your efforts in these areas.   Review of applications will begin on October 5, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Questions about this position may be directed to Adi Dubash, Associate Professor of Biology ( adi.dubash@furman.edu ).   Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--or-Professor-of-French-with-a-specialization-in-African-Francophone-Studies_R003356": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Professor of French with a specialization in African Francophone Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate, or Professor of French with a specialization in African Francophone Studies Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Modern Languages & Literatures Job Summary: The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor of African Francophone Studies to begin August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a thriving French program marked by rapid growth in majors, rich opportunities for experiential learning, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence. We seek an innovative, dynamic teacher-scholar to develop a curricular focus on the Francophone African world. We are inviting candidates with expertise in Francophone Africa and/or the Francophone African Diaspora who will successfully engage students at all levels of French language courses as well as in a variety of advanced-level content courses within the French major. Area of specialization within African Francophone Studies is open and could include expertise in subfields such as ecocriticism, film, new media, digital humanities, cultural studies, gender and sexuality studies, race and ethnicity studies, or literature. Other subfields and topics are also welcomed. Job Description: The teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. The successful candidate will become an integral part of both the French program and the department of Modern Languages and Literatures at Furman. They will be expected to develop courses in their area of expertise, be actively involved in co-curricular programming and French Language House supervision, play an active role in French program recruiting efforts, coordinate study abroad as needed, and teach first-year seminar courses. The successful candidate is also expected to maintain an active research agenda, advise, mentor, become an energetic contributor to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ) and undergraduate research, and participate in department/university service. Qualified candidates must demonstrate a commitment to and excellence in undergraduate instruction at all levels as well as excellence in research, with a promising record of publications. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in French and Francophone Studies, or a related field, expected by August 1, 2027. A minimum of two years of experience teaching at the university level is preferred. Native or near-native level language proficiency in French and English is required. The position offers competitive salary and benefits. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Application instructions: Applicants should submit materials no later than November 1st, 2026. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Applications received after November 1st will be reviewed on a rolling basis until November 20th. While we encourage excellent applicants to submit their completed materials at any point, we cannot guarantee full consideration of late applications. Please upload all application materials as a single PDF in the following order : letter of interest, CV, statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of excellence in teaching (of no more than 10 pages), a writing sample of no more than 20 pages, and contact information for three references (at least one of which must be able to address the candidate’s teaching abilities). References will be contacted at later stages of the search for candidates who advance. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Ronald J. Friis, Chair, Department of Modern Languages and Literatures, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Japanese--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003312": {
      "title": "Professor of Japanese (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Japanese (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Asian Studies Job Summary: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Japanese to begin August 2027. The position consists primarily in teaching Japanese language, and candidates must demonstrate significant experience, excellence, and enthusiasm in Japanese language instruction. We seek applicants with expertise in the fields of Japanese culture and society, including but not limited to film or performing arts, literature, gender and sexuality, or race and ethnicity. Candidates who also possess training in language pedagogical methods are especially encouraged to apply. Teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. Responsibilities also include developing courses in the candidate’s area of specialty, coordinating study abroad; involvement in co-curricular activities; teaching first-year seminars; pursuing an active research agenda; advising and mentoring; and university service. Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. in Japanese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native language proficiency or near-native language proficiency in Japanese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate both excellence in teaching and scholarly potential. Job Description: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Japanese to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a vibrant, interdisciplinary program and a strong commitment to engaged learning. The position consists primarily in teaching Japanese language, and candidates must demonstrate significant experience, excellence, and enthusiasm in Japanese language instruction. We seek applicants with expertise in the fields of Japanese culture and society, including but not limited to film or performing arts, literature, gender and sexuality, or race and ethnicity. Candidates who also possess training in language pedagogical methods are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will become an integral part of the Japanese language program at Furman. Teaching load is five courses per year, which will include language classes at all levels. Responsibilities also include developing courses in the candidate’s area of specialty, coordinating study abroad; involvement in co-curricular activities; teaching first-year seminars; pursuing an active research agenda; advising and mentoring; and university service. Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. in Japanese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native language proficiency or near-native language proficiency in Japanese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate both excellence in teaching and scholarly potential. Successful candidates will also show the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ) and to promoting a diverse and inclusive teaching environment. The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Application instructions: Applicants must submit materials no later than September 20, 2026 as part of the application process. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Inquiries may be directed to Alexander Francis-Ratte, Chair of the Japanese Search Committee, Department of Asian Studies, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613, alexander.francis-ratte@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/IACH-Research-Assistant_R003337": {
      "title": "IACH Research Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: IACH Research Assistant Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: IACH Community Action Job Summary: The IACH is hiring a Research Assistant to support IACH research and evaluation projects with our community and clinical health partners. The position will assist with research activities such as scheduling meetings and taking meeting minutes, IRB submission and amendments, literature reviews, data collection, data cleaning, descriptive data analysis, and reporting. Job Description: Schedules study meetings with external partners and assists the project lead with the development of meeting agendas and meeting minutes. Supports the development and amendment of IRB applications. Supports the development of study instruments including surveys, focus group guides, and interview guides. Assists with the literature reviews and scoping reviews. Collects qualitative and quantitative data following study protocols. Enters and manages study data in RED Cap, Qualtrics, and other data management platforms. Cleans data and conducts descriptive statistics under the supervision of project leads for reports, presentations, and academic products such as conference abstracts and manuscripts. Supports the development of peer reviewed manuscripts. Coordinates with research and evaluation project leads as needed to ensure study timelines and deliverables are met. Assists with logistics and operations such as administering study incentives or processing qualitative transcripts. Participates as a member of the Community Action team and attends relevant IACH meetings. Maintains research professionalism and exercises good judgement when handling sensitive data. Employees may be requested to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically present in the description.  Relationships : Continuous contact with members of own work unit to plan, coordinate, problem solve, exchange information, and make suggestions related to mutual and institutional goals. Frequent interaction with IACH partners to exchange information, engage in creative problem solving and conduct collaborative evaluations. Responsibility for Final Decisions : Responsible for own work.  Reviews work to ensure compliance with policies, procedures, and deadlines. Education/Skill Requirements : Bachelor’s degree in public health, social work, or other health related field required. At least one year of previous experience in applied health research or program evaluation required Effective oral and written communication skills     Strong organizational skills and ability to balance deliverables across multiple project Good analytical and problem-solving skills Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Off-Campus/Child-Development-Center-Substitute-Teacher_R003338": {
      "title": "Child Development Center Substitute Teacher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Child Development Center Substitute Teacher Job Family: Temp Full-Time/Part-Time: Part time Pay Type: Hourly Department: JM Child Development Center Job Summary: To implement the educational program for preschool and/or kindergarten students at Furman’s Child Development Center, using knowledge of child development and best practices. Job Description: Furman University is now accepting applications for an energetic, experienced substitute for preschoolers and kindergartners.  Applicants must have prior experience working with young children in a childcare setting.  A substitute would be contacted as needed and would be responsible for following classroom lesson plans and all guidelines set forth by DSS licensing and the CDC director.  Please submit application, a resume and two letters of reference for consideration. Hours: Variable from 7:30am-5:30pm, as needed Monday-Friday Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Philosophy_R003339": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Philosophy Job Summary: The Department of Philosophy at Furman University invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Philosophy, beginning August 1, 2027. Area of Specialization: History of Philosophy (Ancient Greek and Roman Philosophy, Medieval and Renaissance Philosophy, Arabic and Islamic Philosophy, or Early Modern Philosophy); Area of Competence: Open. The department has need for courses across a wide range of pre-19th century contexts, so candidates who can teach in more than one historical period would be particularly welcome. In addition to their areas of specialized research, the successful candidate will have broad philosophical interests and will be a dynamic and engaging teacher committed to working with students with diverse interests and backgrounds. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach five courses per academic year, including both introductory and upper-level offerings. All members of the department are expected to teach at least one section of “Introduction to Philosophy” annually, as well as periodic First-Year Writing (FYW) seminars on a topic of the candidate’s choosing. The department will be particularly interested in candidates whose teaching engages the history of philosophy in innovative ways, with the potential for intersections with one or more of Furman’s interdisciplinary minors. Furman University is a selective private liberal arts and sciences college. Furman professors are exceptional teacher-scholars who mentor undergraduate students within a campus community that values and encourages diverse ideas and perspectives. A Ph.D. in Philosophy is required by August 1, 2027. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and evidence of innovative teaching. In addition, please arrange for three letters of reference to be sent on your behalf, either by mail or email to david.fink@furman.edu . The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. In addition, please include teaching evaluations (if available), sample syllabi (if available), and at least one writing sample (preferably single-authored). Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and consistently ranked among “America’s Ten Best” by  Forbes . The city boasts a vibrant downtown with top-tier restaurants, parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. It also features an extensive network of nonprofits, international corporations, and excellent public and private schools. The surrounding region offers abundant outdoor recreation, including lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is just 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. A 20-mile bike and pedestrian trail connects Furman’s campus to downtown Greenville and to the nearby town of Travelers Rest—named one of “America's Coolest Small Towns.” The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg International Airport, located just 25 minutes from campus, offers daily service to major cities. Review of applications will begin on October 16 and continue until the position is filled.   Questions may be directed to the Chair of the Philosophy Department, Professor David Fink:  david.fink@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Professor-of-Chinese--Assistant-Associate-Full-_R003322": {
      "title": "Professor of Chinese (Assistant/Associate/Full)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Professor of Chinese (Assistant/Associate/Full) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Asian Studies Job Summary: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Chinese to begin August 2027. Candidates must demonstrate a record of effective teaching and student engagement in Chinese language instruction. The successful candidate will also teach courses in their field of Chinese Studies (specialization open) to complement our departmental offerings, such as cultural studies, film, literature, or other related fields. The successful candidate will teach five courses per year, which will include language classes at various levels and content courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Responsibilities also include collaborating with colleagues to strengthen and expand the Chinese program through curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, and shared program coordination. The position is also responsible for directing study abroad, teaching first-year seminars, offering interdisciplinary courses on Asian Studies, pursuing an active research agenda, and performing university service. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a strong commitment to engaged learning and interdisciplinary teaching. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in Chinese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native or near-native fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and promoting an engaged and inclusive teaching environment and show strong potential for scholarly achievement. Successful candidates will also demonstrate the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage (https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/). The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Job Description: The Department of Asian Studies at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of assistant, associate, or professor of Chinese to begin August 2027. Candidates must demonstrate a record of effective teaching and student engagement in Chinese language instruction. The successful candidate will also teach courses in their field of Chinese Studies (specialization open) to complement our departmental offerings, such as cultural studies, film, literature, or other related fields. The successful candidate will teach five courses per year, which will include language classes at various levels and content courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Responsibilities also include collaborating with colleagues to strengthen and expand the Chinese program through curriculum development, student advising and mentoring, and shared program coordination. The position is also responsible for directing study abroad, teaching first-year seminars, offering interdisciplinary courses on Asian Studies, pursuing an active research agenda, and performing university service. The successful candidate will join one of the largest Asian Studies departments among liberal arts undergraduate institutions, with a strong commitment to engaged learning and interdisciplinary teaching. Qualifications include a Ph.D. in Chinese or a related field expected by Aug 1, 2027. Native or near-native fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and promoting an engaged and inclusive teaching environment and show strong potential for scholarly achievement. Successful candidates will also demonstrate the potential to be dedicated contributors to The Furman Advantage ( https://www.furman.edu/furman-advantage/ ). The position offers competitive salary and benefits. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Application instructions: Applicants must submit materials no later than October 1, 2026 through this link on the Furman University application portal: [     ]. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Preliminary interviews will be conducted remotely via video conference. Inquiries may be directed to Dongming Zhang, Chair of the Chinese Search Committee, Department of Asian Studies, Furman University, 3300 Poinsett Highway, Greenville, SC 29613, dongming.zhang@furman.edu . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Tocqueville-Center-Assistant-Director-and-Assistant-Professor-of-Classical-Liberal-Thought_R003269": {
      "title": "Tocqueville Center Assistant Director and Assistant Professor of Classical Liberal Thought",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Tocqueville Center Assistant Director and Assistant Professor of Classical Liberal Thought Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Tocqueville Center Job Summary: The Tocqueville Center at Furman University invites applications for the position of Assistant/Associate Director, with a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor in Classical Liberal Thought, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek candidates with expertise in the history of liberal thought, particularly focusing on eighteenth- and nineteenth-century British, French, and American Enlightenment thinkers. Job Description: The successful candidate will teach four courses per academic year, including both introductory and upper-level offerings, and will carry out administrative responsibilities at the Tocqueville Center. These duties include student programming and mentorship, event coordination, and media outreach. Furman University is a selective private liberal arts and sciences college. Furman professors are exceptional teacher-scholars who mentor undergraduate students within a campus community that values and encourages diverse ideas and perspectives. A Ph.D. in Political Thought or a related field is required by August 1, 2027. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. In addition, please include teaching evaluations (if available), sample syllabi (if available), and at least one writing sample (preferably single-authored). Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. The  Tocqueville Center for the Study of Democracy and Society  promotes the core principles of a free society—individual liberty, limited government, and freedom of speech—through rigorous academic inquiry. Established in 2008 as a program within the Department of Politics and International Affairs, the Center has since grown into an independent academic unit, gaining greater autonomy, interdisciplinary scope, and programmatic flexibility. This transition has allowed the Center to expand its influence across campus and disciplines. It plays a central role in fostering viewpoint diversity and scholarly engagement, most visibly through its prominent speaker series. The Tocqueville Fellows Program, a fully endowed, interdisciplinary initiative, supports 25 undergraduate students who engage year-round with visiting scholars and classic texts in intimate seminar settings. The Center’s recent elevation reflects the strong backing of Furman’s president and Board of Trustees and affirms the university’s commitment to increasing its national impact. For more information, consult the Center’s website at: https://www.furman.edu/academics/tocqueville-program/ Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and consistently ranked among “America's Ten Best” by  Forbes . The city boasts a vibrant downtown with top-tier restaurants, parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. It also features an extensive network of nonprofits, international corporations, and excellent public and private schools. The surrounding region offers abundant outdoor recreation, including lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is just 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. A 20-mile bike and pedestrian trail connects Furman’s campus to downtown Greenville and to the nearby town of Travelers Rest—named one of “America's Coolest Small Towns.” The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg International Airport, located just 25 minutes from campus, offers daily service to major cities. Review of applications will begin on October 2nd and continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to the search committee co-chairs: Professor Brent Nelsen: brent.nelsen@furman.edu Professor David Fink: david.fink@furman.edu Education Requirements: Doctorate: Political Science (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Mathematics--in-support-of-Data-and-Decision-Analytics-_R003222": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Mathematics (in support of Data and Decision Analytics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant/Associate/Professor of Mathematics (in support of Data and Decision Analytics) Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Mathematics Job Summary: The Department of Mathematics at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level, beginning in the fall 2027 semester. The successful candidate will primarily support the department’s new major in Data and Decision Analytics, which emphasizes coursework and scholarship in statistics, operations research, probability, modeling, and simulation. Job Description: The Department of Mathematics at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level, beginning in the fall 2027 semester. The successful candidate will primarily support the department’s new major in Data and Decision Analytics, which emphasizes coursework and scholarship in statistics, operations research, probability, modeling, and simulation.  Our department is particularly interested in candidates holding a Ph.D. in statistics, operations research, or industrial and systems engineering. Candidates with a Ph.D. in mathematics or applied mathematics are also welcome to apply. All applicants should demonstrate a clear interest in and evidence of teaching and scholarship aligned with our Data and Decision Analytics major. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in a relevant field by August 1, 2027, and provide evidence of teaching excellence, scholarship, and effective institutional service.    Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Chemistry_R003326": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Chemistry Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Chemistry Job Summary: The Department of Chemistry at Furman University invites applications to fill a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the area of inorganic chemistry to begin in August 2027. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in inorganic chemistry or a closely related field with postdoctoral experience strongly preferred. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. Primary teaching responsibilities will be inorganic and general chemistry courses, with additional opportunities to teach advanced topics in the area of research specialization, lab-centered major’s courses, and chemistry for non-majors. The standard teaching load is 4-5 courses per academic year. Tenure-track faculty normally devote their summers to research with students and do not teach. Job Description: The Department of Chemistry at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor.  A Ph.D. in inorganic chemistry or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; prior university-level teaching experience and post-doctoral experience are highly preferred but not required.  The successful candidate will join a vibrant and supportive department of 13 research active faculty.  Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching, service, and scholarship. Furman has a strong history of excellent teaching and mentoring, including a vigorous year-round research program with undergraduate students. Therefore, a faculty member is expected to establish a nationally competitive undergraduate research program. In support of this program, the department maintains state-of-the-art facilities with exceptional instrument holdings, including those in support of inorganic synthetic, photophysics, and materials research, among others.  Furman offers competitive start-up funds, individual research space, and summer support.   Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education.We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest addressing your qualifications and commitment to a research active, undergraduate program. Include a description of how your teaching, scholarship, mentoring and/or service would contribute to a liberal arts college community (2 pages max); a complete curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching and research mentoring philosophy (2 pages max), a detailed research plan (4 pages max), and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, and strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) .  Position commences August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  Education Requirements: Doctorate: Chemistry (Required) Education Requirements: Doctorate: Chemistry (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Financial-Aid-Counselor_R003327": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-07\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Financial Aid Counselor Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Financial Aid-2 Job Summary: The Financial Aid Counselor, under the direction of the Associate Director of Financial Aid, is responsible for advising on financial aid, including awarding federal, state, local, private, and institutional aid to students. The Financial Aid Counselor must stay informed of current financial aid policies and regulations for proper awarding and disbursement of financial aid. Job Description: Position Responsibilities: Research and interpret student financial aid program guidelines including but not limited to those in the Federal Register, student aid handbooks, and training manuals to ensure compliance with federal and state regulations and program requirements. Meet with students and parents concerning the financial aid process and deadlines for applying for aid according to established procedures, and assist in completing the required forms. Provide friendly and knowledgeable assistance to applicants throughout the process. Advise students and parents of requirements and processes. Give clear and concise directions about awarding to students and how the process of allocating funds to their accounts occurs. Assist with the processing of loan files and corrections on a timely basis with accuracy within PowerFAIDS, ELM, and Common Origination Disbursement (COD). Award loans to student accounts and adjust awards as needed. Continue to work as a team member to back up for PowerFAIDS and EDConnect processing when others are not available. Counsel students concerning satisfactory academic progress, withdrawals, and enrollment plans when related to all South Carolina state aid. Counsel students regarding their grade point average and credit requirements and the effects of any dropped, failed, or withdrawals on their South Carolina state aid eligibility. Reconcile state aid programs monthly. Ensure the funds received from the state match the disbursed funds in PowerFAIDS and Workday. Operate all financial aid software programs. Perform data entry and processing. Review, analyze, and package student awards according to institutional, state, and federal requirements as it pertains to all financial aid funds. Understand and articulate the student aid awarding process. Advise current and prospective students, parents, and other interested persons about financial aid programs and requirements. Conduct financial aid workshops and training sessions. Be available to travel and work a flexible schedule as needed to assist in institutional effectiveness. Analyze and evaluate the results of need analysis to accurately determine maximum financial need and aid eligibility for students. Stay abreast of conditions that affect financial aid eligibility. Participate in national, regional, and state conferences on student financial aid programs, practices, and related technology and communicate any information that may be needed by other Furman University departments. Other duties as assigned. Relationships:   Continuous contact with members of multiple work units and immediate supervisor to plan, coordinate, problem solve, exchange information, and make suggestions related to mutual goals. Daily contact with students, parents, faculty, staff, and the public to plan, coordinate, problem-solve, present information, and make suggestions related to mutual goals. Responsibility for Final Decisions :   Reviews work to ensure compliance with procedures and deadlines. Work is performed independently on routine work, non-routine issues or questions are referred to the supervisor. Reports to/ Supervisor: Reports to the Associate Director of Financial Aid Required Education, Skills, and Training: Bachelor’s degree and experience in higher education administration. Friendly, engaging, and excited to help any and all members of the university community. Exacting attention to detail. Significant computer background including experience with relational databases. Strong organizational skills. Effective communication skills, including clear and concise writing. Ability to adapt and respond positively to an ever-changing workplace. Work Conditions : Work is performed under usual office conditions. Education Requirements: Bachelors (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Professor-of-Women-s--Gender--and-Sexuality-Studies_R003319": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Women’s Gender and Sexuality Studies Job Summary: Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies at Furman University invites applications for an Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of WGSS beginning August 1, 2027. Job Description: Job Description : Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies encourages applications from candidates who demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student mentoring/advising, and research in a liberal arts environment. We seek broadly-trained applicants with expertise in global/transnational feminisms as well as intersectional feminist and queer methods and theories. We are especially interested in candidates whose research falls outside of the United States with a preference for a focus on the Global South. Preference will be given to candidates who have conducted teaching and/or research in two one or more of the following areas: disability studies, transgender studies, community-engaged activism, Black or Indigenous feminisms, medicine, science or technology. The teaching responsibility is five courses per academic year. In addition to teaching Introduction to WGS, the candidate will be prepared to teach feminist and queer theory, courses in their area of expertise, and potentially a rotating senior seminar. Candidates may also contribute to teaching across the curriculum through our Pathways and First-year writing programs. We are interested in applicants who will be highly engaged citizens of the university and make meaningful contributions to a young but rapidly growing program. Successful candidates will bring diverse perspectives and provide a rich and varied educational experience for our students. Preferred Qualifications: A PhD in WGS in hand by August 1, 2027. Minimum Qualifications: A graduate certificate in WGS and a PhD in a field closely related to WGS in hand by August 1, 2027. Furman University is a selective private liberal arts and sciences college. Furman professors are exceptional teacher-scholars who mentor undergraduate students within a campus community that values and encourages diverse ideas and perspectives. Our strategic vision, The Furman Advantage, promises students an individualized four-year pathway facilitated by a team of mentors and infused with a rich and varied set of high impact experiences outside the classroom that include undergraduate research, study away, internships, community-focused learning, and opportunities to engage across differences. How to Apply: Applicants are required to submit the following documents electronically in a single PDF: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy and research interests (no more than 4 pages total), a sample “Introduction to WGS” syllabus, and contact information for three references. Applicants should arrange to have three letters of reference submitted on their behalf. The teaching and research statement should describe how your teaching experiences and research agenda would contribute to a small liberal arts community. You may also discuss any relevant professional development, publications, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Furman University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. Domestic partners of employees are eligible for comprehensive benefits. Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Questions can be directed to the chair of the search committee, Kathleen Casey, at kathleen.casey6@furman.edu. About Furman University: Furman University is a private college dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education (FUture Focused). We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. Furman is located in Greenville, SC, one of the fastest growing cities in the Southeast in the fastest growing state in the nation. Greenville has a thriving downtown, 26-mile trail pathway, excellent schools and restaurants, and a vibrant international community. It is located 60 miles south of Asheville, NC. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Lieutenant_R003318": {
      "title": "Lieutenant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Lieutenant Job Family: Service Workers Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Hourly Department: Police Reserve Job Summary: Under general direction, this position works in the area of the University Police Department as a certified Class 1 Constable. Serves as a leader within the Police Department and managing the general police services for an entire squad, both A and B shifts. Position is responsible for planning, organizing, directing and supervising the daily administrative and operational activities of a squad and supervising the enforcement of federal, state and local laws, along with University rules and regulations to maintain order and ensure a safe and orderly environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors. The scope of the position is to maintain order, protect life, safety and property; enforce University regulations, and state and federal laws; and provides general public safety assistance to students, faculty, staff and visitors at Furman University as a state certified Class 1 Constable Job Description: Job Duties: 1.    Ensure efficient and effective routine daily operation of assigned squad. Assist subordinates in performance of duties; review cases with subordinates as appropriate, and provide guidance and direction. 2.    Ensure compliance with the Campus Safety (Jeanne Clery) Act and Title IX. 3.    Interact routinely with and provide assistance to members of the University community, visitors and allied first responders, i.e.: fire, medical and other police personnel; assist allied criminal justice agencies in the service of criminal and civil subpoenas and other court orders. 4.    Deter and prevent crime by patrolling buildings, facilities, properties and other areas in the immediate vicinity of Furman University; observe, report and/or remedy unsafe or problem situations and assist in identifying health and safety hazards.   5.    Respond promptly to calls for service, including: alarms, requests for medical assistance, critical incidents, traffic collisions, reports of criminal activity and other emergencies/non-emergencies; complaints; and criminal activity; conduct searches of persons, places and things possibly seizing and impounding property and evidence where appropriate.; arrest, detain, or subdue resisting offenders using justified and reasonable force where appropriate;  mediate disputes; conduct investigations as appropriate; and communicate vital information including emergency messages as required. 6.    Protect crime scenes; conduct face to face and phone interviews; observe, gather records, process and preserve evidence; present testimony and evidence in court. 7.    Prepare detailed written reports and review and approve written reports from squad.  8.    Plan and organize campus safety and security procedures; provide public awareness and community education presentations. 9.    Perform special services to include: providing personal welfare and money escorts, and unlocking rooms or buildings, etc.; direct traffic and/or parking activities; enforce motor vehicle operation and traffic regulations; assist motorists to resolve vehicle problems; perform crowd control and civil emergency response duties. 10.    Participate in the preparation of the department budget and manage allocation of resources. 11.    Develop department long-range goals, objectives and strategic plans.                      12.    Complete performance review process with supervisor and employees to understand job performance expectations and fit into the department and university goals. 13.    Perform other duties as assigned. The intent of this job classification description is to provide a representative summary of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions in this classification and shall not be construed as a declaration of the specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position. Employees may be requested to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically present in this description. Relationships: Work contacts include administrators, faculty, students, staff, the public and personnel from a variety of local, state and federal criminal justice agencies, and other allied public safety personnel, i.e.: fire, medical, etc. Responsibility for Final Decisions: Provides supervision over both sworn and non-sworn personnel; manages, plans, directs and schedules the work of police department personnel; assures compliance with Furman University Police Department mission, goals, policies, regulations, directives and general orders; conducts short and long-term planning, organization and staffing; provides training, counsels subordinates on employee performance matters and recommends corrective action as appropriate.  May also serve as the acting assistant chief in the absence of the University Assistant Chief. Reports To:  Assistant Chief of Police Receives general direction regarding routine and standard matters and specific instructions regarding non-routine and sensitive matters.  A cooperative reporting relationship with the University President, campus administrators, or designee is required. Minimum Qualifications: Associates Degree, in a related field and five or more years of progressively responsible supervisory/leadership experience; or any relevant combination of education, training and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills and abilities. An example of this would be a South Carolina peace officer certificate or experience as a peace officer for a law enforcement agency in another state or with the federal government and whose training conforms to the basic course of this state. Valid and unrestricted State of South Carolina Driver's License. Active South Carolina Police Academy certification (or equivalent out-of-state certification) and active SC Class 1 Constable commission, or ability to obtain prior to employment or within one year of service as a condition of employment. Certified in First Aid, CPR and AED.      Ability to operate a computer and related software. Knowledge of basic fire protection and control techniques as well as ability to apply them in emergency situations. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, employees and the general public. Knowledge of: organizational leadership principles, current trends in law enforcement, risk, hazard and vulnerability assessment,  South Carolina law; law enforcement practices and techniques consistent with training at a POST certified law enforcement training academy; institutional security measures. Employee supervision, development and performance management skills. Ability to: learn and interpret University policies and procedures to be enforced; respond appropriately to sensitive and emergency situations; communicate effectively; train and direct the work of Police Officer, Police Sergeants, and non-certified Police Department personnel and other University personnel; establish cooperative working relationships with persons contacted in the course of performing assigned duties. Preferred Qualifications:  Bachelor’s Degree. Experience within a campus police department. Working knowledge of the Jean Clery Act and Title IX. Work Conditions:     Will be subject to rotating shifts, unusual work hours, and \"on call\" work; standing and walking for extended periods of time; personal danger while enforcing the laws and dealing with emergency situations; and exposure to disease in the administration of first aid Regular exposure to outside weather conditions. Required to lift a 165 lb. body unassisted.    Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Professor-Sociology_R003292": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant Professor of Sociology Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Sociology Job Summary: The Department of Sociology at Furman University invites applications for two Assistant/Associate/Professor tenure-track positions beginning August 1, 2027. We welcome candidates from any substantive area of sociology whose expertise complements and expands our existing departmental strengths, and whose work reflects a commitment to rigorous inquiry and meaningful engagement with students. A Ph.D. in Sociology is required by August 1, 2027. Job Description: We encourage applications from candidates who demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and research in a liberal arts environment. The teaching responsibility is five courses per academic year.  A strong application will articulate how the candidate envisions contributing to our core curriculum, which includes Introduction to Sociology, Sociological Theory, Qualitative and Quantitative Methods, and 200-level courses in the Sociology of Gender and Sexuality, Race/Ethnicity, or Social Class. Beyond core requirements, we welcome applicants who would bring new course offerings that deepen and diversify our curricular landscape and contribute to the goals of Furman University’s Strategic Plan. Applicants should submit the following documents in a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Additional materials may be requested at later stages of the search process for candidates who advance. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Review of applications will begin on September 10, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct inquiries to Kristy Maher, Acting Chair of Sociology, at kristy.maher@furman.edu Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Classics_R003313": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full  Professor of Classics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Classics Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Classics Job Summary: The Department of Classics at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Classics, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek a broadly-trained classicist with expertise in any of the following areas: Latin prose, Roman history, social history, historiography, Tacitus, Cicero. Job Description: The Department of Classics welcomes applications from candidates who value as we do an integrated approach to teaching, collaborative learning, and scholarship. We seek a broadly-trained classicist with expertise in any of the following areas: Latin prose, Roman history, social history, historiography, Tacitus, Cicero. Candidates must have a thoughtful approach to teaching Greek and Latin, to the rigorous application of technology to humanism, and to engaging the broadest possible community in the study of the ancient world.  Applicants should be prepared to teach a wide range of undergraduate courses in our curriculum, including Greek and Latin at all levels of instruction and thematic courses in classical civilization and culture. The teaching load is five courses over two semesters. Other duties include mentoring and collaborating with undergraduate students on research projects, and contributing to the administrative responsibilities of the Department and the University. A Ph.D. in Classics or a related field is required by August 1, 2027. The deadline for application is October 31, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately. We will conduct initial interviews by Zoom in late November or early December.  Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Randall Childree ( randall.childree@furman.edu ).  Required Documents Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: 1. Letter of interest 2. C.V. 3. Statement of teaching philosophy, and 4. Complete contact information for three references. In the letter of interest, describe how you would teach an upper-level Latin language course and a topical Roman-themed course aimed at the general-education student, and how you would foster undergraduate research. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” (FUture Focused). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or that demonstrate your efforts in these areas. About Furman University Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education.  We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Professor-of-Analytics_R003303": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Analytics Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Business/Accounting Job Summary: The Business and Accounting Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Analytics at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. This position is one of three newly approved faculty hires in business and accounting and will commence on August 1, 2027. Candidates with a strong interest in data analytics education within a nationally ranked liberal arts and science setting are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The teaching load is five courses per year. In addition to the introductory and intermediate business analytics courses, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced data analytics electives related to their area of expertise. Job Description: A Ph.D. or D.B.A. in data analytics, operations, business, or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided the degree is conferred before that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and corporate or industry experience are highly preferred but not required.  The teaching load is five sections per academic year.  In addition to the introductory business analytics course, the candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced business analytics electives related to their area of expertise. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. Duties also include service to the department and university. The Business and Accounting Department offers bachelor’s degrees in Accounting, Business, and Finance . Within the Business major, students can select a track in Entrepreneurship, Marketing, International Business, or Business Administration. The Business and Accounting Department also participates in and supports the Data and Decision Analytics major, and the interdisciplinary minors in Data Analytics and Visual Strategy. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The ideal candidate will also be eager to develop high-impact, engaged learning experiences, including directing and mentoring undergraduate research and course-related projects. The department has a history of community engaged learning. There are currently 10 full-time business and accounting faculty members.  The Joe & Diana Hurley Finance & Business Analytics Lab provides students and faculty with access to Bloomberg terminals and Capital IQ. Faculty receive robust research support, including access to statistical analysis tools such as SAS, STATA, SPSS, and ArcGIS, alongside institutional subscriptions to The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg news. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae , statement of teaching philosophy and interests, statement of research, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. While detailing your specific teaching interests discussion of your prior course experience and any industry background that can be leveraged to enhance classroom instruction and student mentorship is welcomed . The position commences on August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately, with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026, and the search will continue until the position is filled.   Please d irect any questions via email to the S earch C ommittee C hair , Dr. Virginia Gerde , a t virginia.gerde@furman.edu. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-of-Accounting_R003302": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Accounting Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Business/Accounting Job Summary: The Business and Accounting Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Accounting at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. This position is one of three newly approved faculty hires in business and accounting and will commence on August 1, 2027. Candidates with a strong interest in accounting education within a nationally ranked liberal arts and science setting are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or publication in outlets valued by active members of the profession or contribute to their discipline in other significant ways. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. The teaching load is five courses per year. The successful candidate will be able to teach both the introductory level course in managerial/financial accounting and advanced courses, including either federal income taxation or managerial accounting. Job Description: A Ph.D. or D.B.A. in accounting or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided the degree is conferred before that date. Prior university-level teaching experience, professional accounting experience, and involvement in relevant professional organizations are preferred but not required.   The teaching load is five sections per academic year.  In addition to the introductory financial/managerial course, the successful candidate will be prepared to teach advanced courses including federal income taxation or managerial accounting. Successful candidates are expected to excel at teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or publication in outlets valued by active members of the profession or contribute to their discipline in other significant ways. Duties also include service to the department and university. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. The successful candidate will also be eager to develop high-impact engaged learning experiences for undergraduates, including directing research, mentoring, and directing students in course-related projects in the community.  The Business and Accounting Department offers bachelor’s degrees in Accounting, Business, and Finance .   Within the Business major, students select a track in Entrepreneurship, Marketing, International Business or Business Administration. The department also participates in interdisciplinary minors in Data Analytics and Visual Strategy, as well as community engaged courses.  There are currently 10 full-time business and accounting faculty members.  The Joe & Diana Hurley Finance & Business Analytics Lab provides students and faculty with access to Bloomberg terminals, and Capital IQ. Faculty receive research support and have access to statistical analysis tools such as SAS, STATA, SPSS, and ArcGIS, alongside institutional subscriptions to The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg news. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae , statement of teaching philosophy and interests, statement of research, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. While detailing your specific teaching interests, discussion of your prior course experience and any industry background that can be leveraged to enhance classroom instruction and student mentorship is welcomed . Position commences August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled.  Direct your questions by email to search committee chair Professor Sandy Roberson, CPA, at sandy.roberson@furman.edu . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Tenure-Track-Position-in-Social-or-Social-CognitivePsychology_R003308": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Position in Social or Social Cognitive Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Tenure-Track Position in Social or Social Cognitive Psychology Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Psychology Job Summary: The Psychology Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Candidates must have expertise in social or social cognitive psychology and be committed to excellent teaching and producing high-quality research with undergraduate collaborators. A Ph.D. in Psychology is required by the position’s start date of August 1, 2027. Job Description: The Psychology Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Candidates must have expertise in social or social cognitive psychology and be committed to excellent teaching and producing high-quality research with undergraduate collaborators. A Ph.D. in Psychology is required by the position’s start date of August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a vibrant and supportive department with outstanding teaching and research resources. Candidates will teach courses in stereotyping, prejudice, and discrimination, along with introductory psychology and research methods and statistics. They may also have the opportunity to teach other courses that support or expand the department’s curriculum, including a first-year writing seminar. The teaching load is five courses per year, split over two semesters. Faculty are also expected to serve as research mentors to undergraduate students throughout the academic year and during the summer. We offer competitive start-up funds, research space, and summer support. Founded in 1826, Furman University is a highly ranked liberal arts college that offers all students an integrated four-year pathway preparing them for lives of purpose and impact. The psychology major is known for its rigorous coursework, exceptional mentoring and advising, and numerous opportunities for high-impact, engaged learning experiences (e.g. research, internships, and travel study) supported by university resources. More information about the department is available at furman.edu/academics/psychology. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external-facing institutes. The successful candidate will have the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity to Furman’s rich learning culture. Furman is located in Greenville, South Carolina, one of the fastest-growing cities in the Southeast and is ranked among \"America's Ten Best\" by Forbes Magazine. The thriving downtown features excellent restaurants, in-town parks, shops, museums, galleries, music venues, and theaters. Greenville also enjoys an impressive network of nonprofits, small businesses, and international corporations. The city also has excellent public and private schools and a vibrant international community. A 20-mile bike and running trail connects the university to Greenville and to Travelers Rest, which was named \"one of America's coolest small towns.\" The surrounding area abounds with outdoor recreational activities and has some of the country's most beautiful lakes, rivers, and mountains. Greenville is 2½ hours from Atlanta, 1½ hours from Charlotte, and only one hour from Asheville, North Carolina. Greenville is within easy reach of the Blue Ridge Mountains and Atlantic Beaches. The newly renovated Greenville-Spartanburg Airport, located just 25 minutes from downtown, runs daily flights to major cities and airline hubs. It is an ideal place to live and work. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, C.V., statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, a statement of scholarly interests, representative publications, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ). You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. Selected candidates will be asked to arrange for 3 letters of recommendation to be submitted. Questions about the position can be sent to Dr. Erin Hahn, Department Chair ( erin.hahn@furman.edu ).   Review of applications begins September 25, 2026. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Associate-Director-for-Housing-Operations_R003287": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Housing Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Associate Director for Housing Operations Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Housing Job Summary: Under the supervision of the Assistant Dean and Director of Housing and Residence Life, the Associate Director for Housing Operations provides leadership for the operation, maintenance, custodial services, and facility stewardship of the University's residential communities. The position oversees daily facility operations, supervises housing facilities personnel, manages vendor and contractor relationships, coordinates maintenance efforts, administers operational budgets, and collaborates with campus partners to provide safe, functional, attractive, and well-maintained living environments that support student success. The Associate Director exercises independent judgment in the daily management of housing operations while advancing departmental and institutional priorities through collaborative leadership, sound decision-making, and exceptional customer service. Job Description: Responsibilities: 1. Leadership & Personnel Management Hires, trains, supervises, develops, and evaluates three Housing Custodial Supervisors and approximately ten custodial and maintenance employees. Establishes performance expectations and promotes a culture of accountability, professionalism, teamwork, continuous improvement, and exceptional customer service. Conducts regular meetings with supervisors to coordinate operations and safety. Oversees employee scheduling, work assignments, attendance, leave management, and daily operational priorities. Ensures compliance with university policies, safety requirements, and on-call responsibilities. Coordinates staff development and completes performance evaluations. Provides leadership during operational change. 2. Facilities Operations & Logistics Oversees operation, maintenance, and custodial services for all residential facilities. Develops preventative maintenance and inspection programs. Conducts routine inspections. Coordinates maintenance with Facilities Services and contractors. Oversees key/access management including KeyTracer. Coordinates purchase and inventory of furnishings and equipment. Coordinates Summer Programs housing support. Oversees opening/closing inspections and damage documentation. Assists with long-term facility renewal and deferred maintenance planning. Recommends operational improvements. 3. Customer Service & Relationship Management Promotes responsive, solution-oriented customer service. Maintains collaborative relationships with campus partners. Represents Housing on facility planning and renovation projects. Develops productive relationships with vendors and contractors. Monitors contractor performance and compliance. Collaborates with Residence Life staff. Communicates effectively with students, families, faculty, and staff. 4. On-Call & Emergency Response Participates in on-call rotation. Oversees Housing Maintenance On-Call Program. Responds to after-hours emergencies. Coordinates emergency response with campus partners. Exercises sound judgment during emergencies. Maintains knowledge of crisis protocols. 5. Administrative & Financial Stewardship Develops and monitors operating budgets. Oversees procurement of supplies, equipment, and contracted services. Evaluates products for cost, sustainability, and durability. Oversees damage assessment processes. Maintains operational records and databases. Assists with contracts and prepares reports. Completes performance review process with supervisor/employees to understand job performance expectations and how they fit into the department and University goals. Performs other duties as assigned by supervisor in support of the goals and objectives of the department and the Division of Student Life. The intent of this job classification description is to provide a representative summary of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions in this classification and shall not be construed as a declaration of the specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position. Employees may be requested to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically present in this description. Relationships: Daily contact with members of the Residence Life team, immediate supervisor, students, and student staff to plan, coordinate, problem solve, and present information related to mutual goals. Develops collaborative relationships with Housing and Residence Life staff, Facilities Services, University Police, Student Life, Procurement, Finance, Environmental Health and Safety, Information Technology, Summer Programs, contractors, vendors, architects, consultants, students, parents, faculty, and staff. Builds relationships grounded in collaboration, trust, accountability, professionalism, and mutual respect. Responsibility for Final Decisions: Exercises independent judgment regarding the daily operation of residential facilities within established university policies. Daily supervision of custodial and maintenance personnel Prioritization of maintenance requests Preventative maintenance and inspections Vendor and contractor oversight Procurement within approved budgets Key control operations On-call scheduling and emergency response Operational recommendations for room damage Allocation of departmental resources Reports to: Assistant Dean and Director of Housing and Residence Life Work is performed independently on routine work; non-routine issues or questions are referred to the supervisor. Education/Skill Requirements: bachelor's degree required. Three to seven years of progressively responsible facilities or housing experience with supervisory experience preferred. Strong leadership, communication, budgeting, project management, customer service, and decision-making skills. Work Conditions: Work is performed in office and residential facility environments. Some evening/weekend work and participation in an on-call rotation required. Education Requirements: Bachelors (Required) Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate-or-Full-Professor-Business_R003300": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance Job Family: Furman Faculty Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Pay Type: Salary Department: Business/Accounting Job Summary: The Business and Accounting Department at Furman University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Finance at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. This position is one of three newly approved faculty hires in business and accounting and will commence on August 1, 2027. Candidates with a strong interest in finance education within a nationally ranked liberal arts and science setting are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The teaching load is five courses per year. In addition to the introductory corporate finance course, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced finance electives related to their area of expertise. Job Description: A Ph.D. or D.B.A in finance or a related discipline is required by August 1, 2027; ABD candidates will be considered, provided the degree is conferred before that date. Prior university-level teaching experience and corporate or financial industry experience are highly preferred but not required.  The teaching load is five sections per academic year.  In addition to the introductory corporate finance course, the candidate will have the opportunity to teach advanced finance electives related to their area of expertise. Successful candidates are expected to excel in teaching at the undergraduate level, mentor and advise students, and conduct original research leading to peer-reviewed publications or other significant scholarly contributions to the discipline. Duties also include service to the department and university. The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the ability to work with students from diverse backgrounds and contribute to Furman’s commitment to expanding access and opportunity within our rich learning culture. The ideal candidate will also be eager to develop high-impact, engaged learning experiences, including directing and mentoring undergraduate research and course-related projects.  The Business and Accounting Department offers bachelor’s degrees in Accounting, Business, and Finance .   Within the Business major, students can select a track in Entrepreneurship, Marketing, International Business, or Business Administration. The department also participates in interdisciplinary minors in Data Analytics and Visual Strategy , as well as community-engaged courses.  There are currently 10 full-time business and accounting faculty members.  The Joe & Diana Hurley Finance & Business Analytics Lab provides students and faculty with access to Bloomberg terminals and Capital IQ. Faculty receive robust research support, including access to statistical analysis tools such as SAS, STATA, SPSS, and ArcGIS, alongside institutional subscriptions to The Wall Street Journal and Bloomberg news. Furman University is dedicated to fostering a vibrant and inclusive community through excellence in teaching, mentorship, and programming. We believe that cultural understanding, inclusiveness, and freedom of inquiry, thought, and discourse are essential components of a transformative undergraduate education. We advance these ideals with a liberal arts and sciences curriculum built on a substantial general education program, featuring traditional and innovative elements, and a robust portfolio of disciplinary and interdisciplinary major and minor areas of study. Additionally, we have established and continue to develop various initiatives, including historic projects, dialogue programs such as On Discourse and the Intergroup Dialogues Program, the Center for Interpersonal Connections, and four distinctive external facing institutes. Applicants should submit the following documents as a single PDF in the order listed: a letter of interest, curriculum vitae , statement of teaching philosophy and interests, statement of research, and complete contact information for three references. The statement of teaching philosophy and interests should describe your inclusive teaching and mentoring efforts, broadly conceived, and how your teaching and mentoring may contribute to a liberal arts and sciences community that aims, among other things, to “honor inquiry, promote diversity, [and] strive for equity” ( FUture Focused ) . You may also discuss any relevant professional development, service contributions, or other experiences that have refined your skills or demonstrate your efforts in these areas. While detailing your specific teaching interests discussion of your prior course experience and any industry background that can be leveraged to enhance classroom instruction and student mentorship is welcomed . The position commences on August 1, 2027. Review of applications will begin immediately, with priority consideration given to applications received by September 15, 2026, and the search will continue until the position is filled.   Please direct any questions via email to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Francis Kim, at francis.kim@furman.edu . Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Associate-Director--Law-Careers-and-Pre-Law-Advising_R003276": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Law Careers and Pre-Law Advising",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Associate Director, Law Careers and Pre-Law Advising Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Compensation Grade: 7S Pay Type: Salary Department: Associate Dean for Mentoring and Advising Job Summary: The Associate Director, Law Careers and Pre-Law Advising is responsible for maintaining an ecosystem of support for students interested in pursuing law careers. The Associate Director serves as the primary point of contact for students exploring or pursuing law careers, providing advising, coaching, and mentoring through individual/group advising that guides students through the process of discerning whether a law career is the right choice, obtaining internships and shadowing opportunities to clarify paths, developing curated resources and programming, and providing support throughout the application process for law school or post-graduate paths. To do this effectively, the Associate Director must collaborate with Furman’s Pre-Law Advisory Group comprised of faculty and staff with experience in law or law-related fields, be student-centered, have a strong commitment to the liberal arts, and actively engage both internal and external stakeholders through effective communications and programming to promote student success. Job Description: Responsibilities: Individual and Group Advising Serves as an expert for law careers, staying up-to-date on trends in the field, timelines for application processes, federal policies that impact law school financing, and educational and co-curricular expectations of recruiting practices Advises students and alumni in one-on-one and group meetings: Connects advisees to the curricular interests, majors/minors, and out-of-class experiences (e.g., Mock Trial, Medical Legal Partnership) that support goals and interests along their individualized pathways Provides information on a wide range of legal careers Counsels on both immediate and long-term personal and professional goals Provides support for resume writing and interview preparation for internships and employment Writes recommendation letters for both on-campus and external programs and activities Represents pre-law advising during orientation events Coordinates pre-law exploratory meetings Facilitates connections with members of the Pre-Law Advisory Group as relates to student interests Provides guidance regarding the law school application process and preparation of the application package for current students and alumni Advises on law school exploration and planning, including helping students discern whether law school is the right choice for them, and what to look for in a law school Advises on LSAT preparation Provides resources and guidelines for and feedback on personal statements, recommendation letters, resumes, and cover letters for current students and recent alumni Provides support for interview preparation for law school applicants Meets with students individually to discuss application and recommendation process Provides post-application support Provides support for prospective students considering pre-law: Serves as the contact person for Enrollment Services to ensure that prospective students and families are connected with the appropriate faculty and resources Facilitates and conducts group information sessions for prospective students Faciliates and conducts information sessions for on-campus Admissions programs and events Responds to emails and phone calls from both prospective students and parents/guardians throughout the year Develops a plan for the assessment of outcomes and advising practices: Tracks student engagement with the office and outcomes, including student acceptances to law school, as well as placement in related fields to determine best practices for pre-law advising Tracks student performance on LSAT exam Solicits and collects feedback on advising process for pre-law students Keeps faculty and relevant administrators advised annually on the success of candidates in the application process Programming & Resources Assists with development, implementation, support, and management of programming to support pre-law student exploration and preparation, and facilitates connections between students and professionals in the field and celebrates successes.  Examples include: External speaker seminar series Alumni panels Community and alumni law professional networking events Career Conversations with alumni and professionals in the field Law Day Celebration of rising 1Ls Cultivates on-going relationships with law school admission officials and the Law School Admission Council (LSAC): Coordinates recruitment visits and presentations by law school admission officials Plans and leads students on visits to law schools and regional law school fairs, as appropriate, to make connections and cultivate relationships with law school admission officials Communicates changes in LSAT preparation and admissions standards and processes to the Pre-Law Advisory Group Acts as an advocate of Furman University as an institution that successfully prepares students for law school as well as an advocate on behalf of Furman’s law school applicants Establishes and maintains online platforms for sharing resources and communicating with pre-law students. This includes: The Pre-Law Advising Moodle page, which acts as a repository of resources for current students (legal field career guides, videos of alumni panels and talks, resources for application steps for law school) The pre-law program website, which acts as an external facing resource for prospective and current students, and alumni Managing a law -focused alumni group in The Furman Network (i.e., PeopleGrove) Using systems for student appointments and information sharing with campus resources (e.g., Handshake) Social media channels Acts as the advisor for the Pre-Law Society (student organization for pre-law students) to develop and deliver effective programming to align with student needs and interests. Collaborates with campus partners, e.g., Mock Trial, Medical Legal Partnership, the Riley Institute for Public Policy and Civic Leadership and other campus Centers and Institutes, to promote existing programs and design relevant collaborative opportunities, where appropriate. Relationship Development & Engagement Develops and maintains relationships with faculty, employers, professional associations, alumni, parents, and graduate schools for advising, networking, programming, and other career exploration purposes for students pursuing careers in law. Collaborates with the Associate Director of Networking and Student Connections to build a network of support for students and alumni pursuing careers in law. This includes developing relationships with alumni and other professionals working in the legal field who are willing to connect with students and alumni for inquiries, career conversations, mock interviews, etc. Works with faculty and staff mentors, alumni, local partners, and relevant administrative offices to develop opportunities to expose students to potential pathways in the legal profession Identifies existing opportunities and markets them to current students and alumni Develops shadowing opportunities for students to explore the field of law Develops internship/externship opportunities for students to obtain hands-on experience Serves as the campus point person to request resources for supporting students pursuing law careers. Provides guidance and support to Furman faculty, academic departments, and administrative offices including but not limited to: Serving as a liaison for the pre-law pathway and consults with faculty to ensure they are updated on the law school admission process and pre-law pathway experiences Works with the Malone Center for Career Engagement in conjunction with the Director of Internship Initiatives and Strategy to develop internships that expose students to potential pathways in the legal profession Works with the Associate Director of Networking and Student Connections and uses the Furman Network (i.e., Peoplegrove) to connect students with alumni mentors who have careers in the legal profession Partners with Associate Directors in the Malone Center for Career Engagement to establish opportunities for co-sponsoring visits by legal experts that intersect with other industry-specific areas Creates guidelines for letters of recommendation and prepares faculty to use those guidelines when writing letters for students. Cross-Functional Teams and University Initiatives Tracks student engagement distributed across categories that include exploration, internships, and connections with other campus resources. Serves as a co-leader of the Pre-Law Advisory Group comprised of faculty and staff with experience in law or law-related fields. Contributes to the Furman University, Malone Center for Career Engagement, and Office of Advising for Health and Law Professions strategic plans. Represents the Division of Academic Affairs and Office of Advising for Health and Law Professions on divisional and university committees. Pursues professional development to ensure effective practices, such as representing Furman University and the Office of Advising for Health and Law Professions Office in local and national professional associations and conferences to stay current with industry standards and network with professionals in higher education and within the legal profession. Performs administrative tasks such as setting appointments, email, phone calls, paperwork, photocopying, organizing, filing, etc. Completes performance review process with supervisor to understand job performance expectations and how they fit into the department and university goals. Performs other duties as assigned. Relationships: Daily contact with students to exchange information to plan, coordinate, solve problems, and present information related to students’ law-related goals. Frequent contact with alumni to exchange information to plan, coordinate, solve problems, and present information related to alumni law-related goals.             Frequent contact with university departments and members of own work unit to plan, coordinate, solve problems, and present information and suggestions related to mutual goals. Frequent contact with faculty and staff to coordinate both on-campus and external events and initiatives related to pre-law and legal careers. Frequent contact with law schools. Requires maintaining a professional relationship as a representative of Furman. Frequent contact with faculty, staff, and advisors to exchange information to plan, coordinate, solve problems, and present information related to mutual goals of supporting students with pre-law interests. Responsibility for Final Decisions: Responsible for own work. May assist or instruct others doing similar work, including student workers.  Tasks involve interpretation of data and/or procedures to address problems or situations that are not clearly defined. Work involves non-routine/diverse work not defined by procedures. Errors may be detected within the department or section in which they occur, but may affect the work of others within the unit to trace errors and make corrections Spends time planning, scheduling, and assigning priorities of several ongoing assignments. Reports To : Director of the Office of Advising for Health and Law Professions Work is performed independently except where the interpretation of law, policy, rule, complex procedure, or request for exception is required. Minimum Qualifications : Juris Doctorate (strongly preferred) or Master’s degree with a minimum of two years experience in a legal setting and/or advising experience in higher education. Strong interpersonal skills, and effective oral and written communication skills. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse constituents, including students, parents, faculty, admissions officers, and administrative staff. Sensitivity to the needs of a diverse student population, including minority and international students. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including occasional evenings and/or weekends.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in legal settings and / or knowledge of the expectations, responsibilities, and accountabilities of legal professionals. Experience with systems such as Workday Student, course management software (e.g., Moodle), Handshake, and PeopleGrove Work Conditions : Work is performed under usual office conditions. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Staff-Piano-Teacher_R003282": {
      "title": "Staff Piano Teacher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Staff Piano Teacher Job Family: Temp Full-Time/Part-Time: Part time Compensation Grade: TMP Pay Type: Hourly Department: JM Music Job Summary: Piano for Young People is a pre-college piano program for students kindergarten through high school. Students pursue piano study through private lessons in a university setting. Materials covered in lessons include sight reading, music theory, music history, ear training, and an introduction to a wide range of musical genres and styles of the teacher and student’s choosing. Staff teachers in Piano for Young People are responsible for teaching weekly lessons on campus, planning and preparing for individualized lessons, sending weekly assignments and reminders to students and parents, meeting with the director as needed, and regular correspondence. Staff teachers also attend recitals and competition events throughout the academic year. Staff teachers are committed to professional development and growth in knowledge of pedagogical practices. Job Description: Teaching Teaches weekly individualized piano lessons to students ages five and older, including sight reading, music theory, music history, ear training, technique, and repertoire. Creates and fosters relationships with students and families. Teaches in person and virtually as required by the program and university. Planning Prepares weekly for lessons through communication with students and parents, writing weekly assignments, and coordinating with the director. Pursues professional development to stay knowledgeable of pedagogical practices. Performs other duties as assigned by the director. Recitals & Events Prepares students for and attends recitals and other performances throughout the academic year. Communication Communicates regularly with students/parents, director, and others. Reports To Director of Piano for Young People Requirements/Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or higher in Music, Piano, or Piano Pedagogy. Prior teaching experience Preferred Knowledge, Abilities, and Skills Knowledge of pedagogical practices, piano method books, and sequencing instruction Adept at working with children Adaptable and open to trying new pedagogical methods Proficient and comfortable with virtual lessons and digital communication Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Grants-and-Contracts-Accountant_R003265": {
      "title": "Grants and Contracts Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Grants and Contracts Accountant Job Family: Professionals Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Compensation Grade: 7S Pay Type: Salary Department: Financial Services Job Summary: The Grants and Contracts Accountant is an integral part of Furman University’s Finance and Administration Division and is responsible for managing the financial administration of externally funded grants and contracts while ensuring compliance with university, sponsor, and governmental regulations. The Grants and Contracts Accountant is responsible for the accounting, monitoring, reporting, and compliance activities related to sponsored research grants, contracts, and other special funding sources. This position works closely with the Grants office, principal investigators (PIs), department administrators, and external funding agencies to ensure proper financial stewardship of awarded funds. Job Description: Responsibilities: Grant and Contract Management Monitor financial activity for federal, state, local, and private grants and contracts. Review expenditures to ensure allowability, allocability, reasonableness, and compliance with sponsor requirements. Establish and maintain grant and contract accounts within the university's Workday system. Reconcile grant and contract accounts on a regular basis based on requirements. Track grant budgets and expenditures to prevent overspending or fund deficits. Communication with PIs and departments when overspending occurs. Recording of receivables and deferred revenue at year-end, providing detailed listings by grant that make up each total for year-end schedules. Financial Reporting Prepare and submit financial reports required by sponsoring agencies. Generate monthly, quarterly, and annual reporting for grant-funded projects in conjunction with preparing invoices for each sponsor and related documentation requirements. Assist departments and principal investigators with budget monitoring and financial analysis. Prepare reports for university leadership regarding sponsored programs. Prepare annual SEFA-Schedule of Expenditures of Federal Awards. Compliance and Audit Support Ensure compliance with federal regulations, including Uniform Guidance (2 CFR Part 200), sponsor requirements, and university policies. Assist with internal and external audits of grants, including the Single Audit, Research & Development cluster when applicable. Maintain supporting documentation and audit trails for all financial transactions. Complete journal entries as needed, and grant closeout activities. Overseeing and monitoring of time and effort reporting for all grants. Budget Development and Analysis Assist faculty and administrators with grant budget preparation. Analyze budget variances and provide recommendations for corrective actions. Ensure sub recipient monitoring analysis is performed and tracked on an annual basis, including SAM.gov debarment requirements are met. Grant Closeout Coordinate financial closeout of grants and contracts. Verify that all expenses have been properly recorded and reported. Prepare final financial reports and reconciliations. Ensure timely return of unspent funds when required. Collaboration and Customer Service Serve as a financial resource for faculty, staff, and department administrators. Provide training and guidance regarding grant accounting procedures and sponsor regulations. Work closely in coordination with the Grants Office and Principal Investigators (PIs). Works daily with members of Financial Services to plan, coordinate, solve problems, and present information and suggestions related to mutual goals. Other Tasks Annual preparation HERD survey Prepare Indirect Cost Proposals Perform physical inventory of equipment purchased with federal funds Drawing down funds from government agencies and sponsors according to prepared invoices and reconciling to the General Ledger. Maintain files for each grant/contract. Assist the Finance team with backup and coverage for other positions as needed. Assists in testing Workday related upgrades and providing training programs for university staff for new or revised processes and procedures. Provides support on special projects and data analysis for the Associate Vice President of Finance, Controller, Director of Budget and Resource Management, and Director of Procurement as needed. Pursues professional development opportunities to keep pace with demands for services and information, including maintaining relevant information about the department and university. Completes the annual performance review process with supervisor to understand job performance expectations and department and university goals. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting or Finance. Two to five years of accounting experience, preferably in higher education, government, nonprofit, or grant accounting. Knowledge of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). Experience with financial reporting and account reconciliations. Proficiency with Excel spreadsheets including pivot tables. Preferred Qualifications Experience with sponsored research accounting in higher education. Knowledge of federal grant regulations and Uniform Guidance. Experience with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems such as Workday. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to interpret grant agreements and sponsor regulations. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple deadlines and priorities. Knowledge of basic principles, concepts and methodology of accounting required. Ability to use independent judgment in planning and controlling non-routine activities. Ability to maintain confidentiality of accounting records. Advanced Excel and financial reporting skills. Relationships Continuous contact with members of own work unit, Financial Services, Facilities Services, Information Technology, Human Resources, President’s Office, Vice Presidents, division directors, and members of other departments to exchange information and explanation of policies, procedures, regulations, acceptable practices and functions.  Developing positive, collaborative working relationships is essential to the success of this position. Clear and concise communication is required to successfully fulfill job duties efficiently and effectively. Reports To: University Controller This position reports directly to the University Controller in the Finance and Administration department with a dotted line reporting structure to Director of Grants and Research Administration. This position will work closely with the Grants Office and receive training, direction and guidance from the Grants office.  Work is performed independently except where the interpretation of law, policy, rule, complex procedure or request for exception is required. Working Conditions Work is performed under usual office conditions with long periods of working at a desk and in front of a computer screen. The Grants Accounting position will be eligible for one or two remote workdays per week after one year of service, with supervisor approval. Responsible for own work. Exercises independent judgement and discretion, as it relates to the application of established University policies and procedures. Routine work is performed independently, involves deadlines, interruptions and handling multiple tasks. Tasks involve multiple procedures with interrelated processes or steps. Work involves choosing the appropriate option or procedure to follow and applying established rules and procedures. Understanding of how workflows are structured is essential to completing work related tasks in a timely manner. Errors are readily detected in the normal course of work by standard check or crosscheck. Follows safety procedures consistent with an office environment. May frequently travel to other parts of the University campus, with infrequent off-campus travel. Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    },
    "https://furman.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Police-Officer_R003248": {
      "title": "Police Officer - Excellent Benefits!",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWelcome to Furman University's Career Site! IMPORTANT :​ Load all documents in the My Experience area under Resume/CV . This may include your resume/C.V., cover letter, unofficial transcript, teaching philosophy, etc. Please wait for all documents to finish uploading before clicking Next. If the process times out you will lose your progress, so please ensure you have all necessary documents available before starting. The drop-down lists only display so many options: please type into a drop-down list to search for your option. For example: in Field of Study, you may need to enter your field name. If you have no field, type \"None.\" If you have previously applied, make sure your information is current as you can transfer it to another application. Prior to submitting your application, verify all information for accuracy and ensure you have uploaded all appropriate documents.  Once submitted, you will not be able to edit your application other than to change your contact information. If you have any questions or need additional assistance, please contact the Office of Human Resources via email at recruitment@furman.edu  or by calling 864-294-3103. Job Title: Police Officer - Excellent Benefits! Job Family: Service Workers Full-Time/Part-Time: Full time Compensation Grade: 5H Pay Type: Hourly Department: Red Squad Job Summary: The Furman University Police Department (FUPD) is the primary department charged with creating a safe and secure environment at Furman University. FUPD operates 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. University Police Officers provides law enforcement, security, public and traffic safety services in an authentic community policing environment. University Police Officers are state certified, commissioned law enforcement professionals reporting directly to a shift sergeant. Officers conducts patrols of campus, investigate or assists with investigations, complete incident reports, assist with prosecutions and testify in court, conduct campus security inspections and secure campus facilities, direct and assist with traffic control, respond to emergencies, and maintain the public trust through positive and effective public relations. Job Description: Benefits: Night Shift Differential - $2 per hour for hours worked between 6 p.m. and 7 a.m. 12-Hour Shifts - 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. or 7 p.m. to 7 a.m. Retention Bonuses ($1,000 at 1 year, $3,000 at 3 years, and $5,000 at 5 years of service) Employee Wellness Program that includes time to work out on duty (when staffing permits) Overtime: limited mandated overtime, but unlimited voluntary overtime opportunities Retirement 403B - Furman contributes 5% of gross after 2 years; 10% of gross after 7 years (100% vested immediately; no match needed) Vacation - 3 weeks accrued during first year Sick Time - 10 days accrued each year  Holidays - 17 paid holidays including 4 floating holidays (plus double time pay for holidays worked) Wellness Hours - 8 hours per month of additional paid leave during summer months Gym Membership - free membership to the Furman fitness center for you and dependents Tuition Benefits - FREE tuition for employee, spouse, and dependent children Medical Insurance - excellent medical insurance through Blue Cross Blue Shield Click HERE For additional information regarding benefits: Job Description and Responsibilities: Among other duties University Police Officers are expected to: Protect life and property through the enforcement of state laws and university regulations. Proactively patrol assigned areas, address observed public safety situations, and respond to calls for service. Monitor and investigate suspicious activity in order to prevent crime and apprehend criminals. Investigate suspected violations of criminal law and university policy. Complete incident reports, aid in the prosecution of crimes, and testify in court as required.  Collect, process, and store property and evidence. Conduct campus security inspections, lock and unlock facilities, monitor and control access to campus and buildings, respond to alarms, inspect facilities and initiate work orders for inoperative or faulty security and safety equipment. Enforce traffic law and campus parking and traffic policies, respond to and investigate traffic collisions, direct traffic, assist motorists, and conduct personal escorts. Provide public safety services and crowd control at special events and campus activities. Participate in crime prevention and crime reduction programs, attend community meetings on problem resolution and service support representing the department. Maintain positive and effective public relations in support of the department and university while in the performance of their duties. Make arrests in accordance with state and federal law and pursuant to department policy, and conduct searches and seizures pursuant to the Fourth Amendment and department policy.  Perform emergency services to include but not limited to:  first-aid, CPR, AED, and Narcan administration; respond to fires and fire alarms; correct and/or report fire and safety hazards; respond to natural and man-made disasters, severe weather problems, and other emergency incidents. Pursue professional development and participate in orientation training, in-service training, field training, and off campus training programs necessary to maintain SCCJA certification, and to enhance professional skills and performance as required by the Chief of Police. Serve as a campus security authority and assist the department with compliance with The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Complete additional tasks as assigned by the supervisor which may include assignments to other duties such as dispatcher, office work, community service staff functions, work in plain clothes assignments, participate in stake-outs or assist training officer. Relationships : Continuous contact with members of own work unit, immediate supervisor, members of other departments, students, general public, and officials/representatives of outside agencies and organizations to exchange factual information and explanation of rules, regulations, practices or functions.  Responsibility for Final Decisions : Tasks involve multiple procedures with interrelated processes or steps.  Work involves choosing the appropriate option or procedure to follow and applying established rules and procedures. Errors are readily detected in the normal course of work by standard check or crosscheck.  Reports To :  Shift Sergeant. Work is performed independently on routine work, non-routine issues or questions are referred to the supervisor. Education/Skill Requirements : Must possess a high school diploma or GED recognized by SLED and the SC Criminal Justice Academy (SCCJA). Must have or obtain a valid SC Driver’s License and a good driving record. Must pass department background investigation. Must have successfully completed the SCCJA basic law enforcement academy, or have the ability to complete the SCCJA basic academy within one year of date of hire.       Must be able to successfully obtain a commission from SLED. Must successfully complete department field training program. Must possess or obtain South Carolina voter’s registration card as required by SLED. Completes physical examination as required by the SCCJA. Work requires: Effective verbal communication skills and ability to de-escalate conflicts. Critical thinking skills and ability to exercise good discretion, judgement and decision making. Exposure to violence and physical confrontations. Safe operation of a motor vehicle. Use of firearms, less lethal weapons, and other special equipment. Frequent reaching and handling. Frequent lifting and carrying. Occasional crouching and crawling. Occasional climbing and balancing. Occasional stooping and kneeling. Occasional walking, standing, and running. Work is performed during all weather conditions. Work hours: 12-hour rotating shifts, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Some overtime required as needed to support daily operations, special security assignments and event support. Hiring Process: Depending on qualifications and experience, applicants may be required to successfully complete the following before selection: Written cognitive ability test Physical ability test as required by the SCCJA Oral board interview Psychiatric screening Polygraph or other test to verify truthfulness Drug screening Background investigation and criminal records check Education Requirements: Certification Requirements: Job Posting End Date (if date is blank, posting is open ended):"
    }
  },
